>> title: Polenta
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: cornmeal, italian, side, cheese, stovetop
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: creamy polenta, polenta cremosa, soft polenta
>> pairs-with: bolognese, braised-short-ribs
>> servings: 6
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: narrow — coarse cornmeal catches on the bottom the moment it is left, and scorched polenta tastes of nothing else

>> step: boil
Bring @water{6%cups}(1.4 L) to a boil in a #heavy saucepan{} with @kosher salt{2%tsp} and @bay leaf{1}.

>> step: whisk in
Whisk @coarse cornmeal{1 1/2%cups}(255 g) into @&(~1)boiling water{} in a slow steady stream.

>> step: stir 40 min
Cook @&(~1)polenta{} over low heat, stirring often, for ~{40%min}, loosening it with @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL) as it thickens.

>> step: beat in off the heat
Beat @grated Parmesan{1%cup}(85 g), @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)polenta{} off the heat.
